Z||000000||STPSTP1||09-16-2001||11:45 PM||||I just got an 87 gt, and i have a stress crack in the driver side back QTR window. Does anyone have any for sale?||||reg||1
Z||000001||SLYGUY||09-17-2001||01:55 AM||||I just got my 88 GT two weeks ago and I have the same problem with the driver's side rear quarter on it. Sounds like the same thing happened to it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I'm going to need a passenger side also. Not cracked the same way though. It has spider stress cracks in it. From about six feet away in the right sunlight it looks like it has a lot of water spots in it.<P>I looked around. You can get a set of NON OEM duplicates for around $200 delivered. Heard that they look very similar but won't stand up to a knowledgeable fiero owner. Heck, they even have a slight green tint and "similar" bend to them. I forget what site had them.<P>You can get original OEM quarters at <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com." TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com.</A> <P>They are expensive though.<BR>$189 each.<BR>Expensive, but that is what I am going to do.<P><BR>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-17-2001||05:09 AM||||Doug Kinney (007Doug) of the Fiero Warehouse sells those repros for $200 delivered.  They might not stand up to a concours judging, but there are alot of us here on PFF that have them and love them.  You can get them as original or with a 20% tint (that's what I bought).  Don't waste your money on the Fiero Stores sail panels unless you MUST have a 100% concours restoration.<P>------------------<BR>In memory of those that died on 11 Sept 2001.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367.gif">  <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||09-17-2001||12:14 PM||||Thanks Monkeyman,<P>I needed that info too<P><BR>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
